        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ExcomI">Excom I</ref> 9</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Excom I 9" corresp="#wit-ti"><pb n="432" ed="#liebermann"/>Et Iohannes dilectus pre cęteris Christi discipulis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="46" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.46"/> talem nefarium hominem salutare prohibet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.47"/>, dicens<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="n" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.n"/>: ‘Ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="48" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.48"/> ei aue dixeris, neque eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.49"/> in domum receperis. Qui enim ei aue dixerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="50" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.50"/>, communicat operibus eius malignis’.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="51" target="#ExcomI_9.lnote.oe.51"/></ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">2 Ioa. 10. 1</note>
